From b05d42eefac737ce3cd80114d3579111023941b8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jianbo Liu <jianbol@nvidia.com>
Date: Thu, 19 Jun 2025 12:48:51 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] xfrm: hold device only for the asynchronous decryption

[ Upstream commit b05d42eefac737ce3cd80114d3579111023941b8 ]

The dev_hold() on skb->dev during packet reception was originally
added to prevent the device from being released prematurely during
asynchronous decryption operations.

As current hardware can offload decryption, this asynchronous path is
not always utilized. This often results in a pattern of dev_hold()
immediately followed by dev_put() for each packet, creating
unnecessary reference counting overhead detrimental to performance.

This patch optimizes this by skipping the dev_hold() and subsequent
dev_put() when asynchronous decryption is not being performed.

Signed-off-by: Jianbo Liu <jianbol@nvidia.com>
Reviewed-by: Cosmin Ratiu <cratiu@nvidia.com>
Signed-off-by: Steffen Klassert <steffen.klassert@secunet.com>

[Ankit: Backported for v6.1.191. dev_hold() moves into the non-crypto_done
branch on top of stable 4d06caedea58 (upstream 1c428b038400). The crypto_done
(async resume) pass no longer takes and drops its own reference; the
reference from the first pass is released by the existing 'if (async)
dev_put()' on the exit paths. This is a prerequisite for the follow-up fix
8045c0df98d4, which does not apply to 6.1.191 without it.]
Signed-off-by: Ankit Jain <ankit-aj.jain@broadcom.com>
---
 net/xfrm/xfrm_input.c | 24 +++++------
 1 file changed, 12 insertions(+), 12 deletions(-)

diff --git a/net/xfrm/xfrm_input.c b/net/xfrm/xfrm_input.c
--- a/net/xfrm/xfrm_input.c
+++ b/net/xfrm/xfrm_input.c
@@ -627,20 +627,20 @@
 		XFRM_SKB_CB(skb)->seq.input.low = seq;
 		XFRM_SKB_CB(skb)->seq.input.hi = seq_hi;
 
-		dev_hold(skb->dev);
-
-		if (crypto_done)
+		if (crypto_done) {
 			nexthdr = x->type_offload->input_tail(x, skb);
-		else
+		} else {
+			dev_hold(skb->dev);
+
 			nexthdr = x->type->input(x, skb);
-
-		if (nexthdr == -EINPROGRESS) {
-			if (async)
-				dev_put(skb->dev);
-			return 0;
-		}
-
-		dev_put(skb->dev);
+			if (nexthdr == -EINPROGRESS) {
+				if (async)
+					dev_put(skb->dev);
+				return 0;
+			}
+
+			dev_put(skb->dev);
+		}
 resume:
 		spin_lock(&x->lock);
 		if (nexthdr < 0) {
